Management in 10 words.

00:12:11.220 --> 00:12:13.950
The first request to
this model succeeds

00:12:13.950 --> 00:12:15.990
with a proper answer
and a response.

00:12:15.990 --> 00:12:17.580
But the second request fails

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:19.200
because of the
token limit policy.

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:22.080
I have exceeded my
allocated token quota,

00:12:22.080 --> 00:12:25.380
and now I'm being
throttled by AI Gateway.

00:12:25.380 --> 00:12:30.900
Now I can also change the
prompt to a hateful prompt,

00:12:30.900 --> 00:12:34.800
such as "I hate you," and
execute the model again.

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:38.220
This time, AI Gateway will
block this request due

00:12:38.220 --> 00:12:42.150
to the compliance of content
safety policies that I applied.

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:43.710
This is considered
a hateful request,

00:12:43.710 --> 00:12:46.470
and AI Gateway successfully
blocks it before it reaches the

00:12:46.470 --> 00:12:48.960
model in the backend.

